# Audit Trail Rule

This project requires a full audit trail of all AI-assisted work per IAEA QA requirement 13.1.6.

## Conversation Logging

At the **end of every conversation that produces changes**, create a log file:

- Path: `audit/conversations/YYYY-MM-DD_<short-slug>.md`
- Use today's date and a concise slug describing the session topic
- If a file with that name already exists, append `_02`, `_03`, etc.

Required sections in the log:

```
# <Title>

**Date:** YYYY-MM-DD
**Session ID:** <conversation identifier if available>

## Objective
<What the user requested>

## Key Decisions
- <Decision 1>
- <Decision 2>

## Files Changed
- `path/to/file.md` — <one-line description>

## Outcome
<Completed | Partial | Deferred> — <any follow-up items>
```

## Plan Logging

When a **plan is created or implemented**, copy the full plan content to `audit/plans/` preserving the original filename.

## Rules

- Never skip audit logging, even for small changes.
- The audit log should be written as the final action before the conversation ends.
- Include the audit log file in the same commit as the changes it documents.
- See `audit/README.md` for full conventions.
